<title>UK: Canada's CMHC sets $500 million five-year bond. [CORRECTED 12:00 GMT]</title>
<headline>Canada's CMHC sets $500 million five-year bond. [CORRECTED 12:00 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers DKB International and Merrill Lynch International.</p>
<p> BORROWER   CANADA MORTGAGE AND HOUSING CORP (CMHC)</p>
<p> AMT    $500 MLN	COUPON     **	  MATURITY    02.APR.02</p>
<p>(Corrects maturity date from April 1).</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE  S-09.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+15 BP</p>
<p> NOTES   ** TO BE PRICED</p>
<p>		S-SHORT FIRST COUPON</p>
<p> MOODY	AA2	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA+	 DENOMS (K) =	   SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ONTARIO   HOME CTRY  CANADA    TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  1.625     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND FIVE-YEAR U.S. TREASURY NOTE NOTES CMHC IS AN AGENT OF HER MAJESTY IN RIGHT OF CANADA, AND THE BONDS CARRY FULL FAITH AND CREDIT OF CANADA AND CONSTITUTE DIRECT UNCONDITIONAL OBLIGATIONS OF AND BY CANADA.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
